          "body": "The dashboard/pruning instructions conflict with the user-approved browser-to-PR product direction. Commit the plan of record and canonical 3.0 specification in the repository, align agent rules, and correct the README's stale feature claims.\n\nStage 0: all six starting queues resolved; PR #11 merged at `0cc243a` after Grok exact-head review and successful required check. This documentation checkpoint enables selective controller restoration while preserving discovery/TUI/coordination. It does not claim any runtime acceptance or release gate is complete. Operating HOLD remains effective.\n\nCanonical mapping: BF3-001-AC01/AC03 and BF3-022-AC02 preparation; complete BF3-001\u2013030 and AT/HF/CF obligations retained by the verbatim spec. No package marked complete.\n\nValidation: `bash scripts/check` under Node 22.23.2/npm 10.9.8 passed (53 Rust tests passed, one ignored benchmark; one frontend unit test, typecheck, bundle freshness, format, clippy and build). Canonical spec SHA-256 matches original: `1d8064b40041e9383b66b790eb8eaa41924657db5f5d1bb0a5373fc5c501b9eb`. Edited documentation passes `git diff --check`; the verbatim specification retains three original Markdown hard-break spaces on lines 4\u20136.\n\nIndependent review must name the exact head and come from a different vendor. Shared-identity review comments are not native GitHub approvals.\n\nbf-author: codex/codex-workbench-integrator\nbf-claim: c-14\n",
